title: Tobias and Mrs Kettle
story: fernhill
description: The two people on the estate — a patrolling groundskeeper whose
  topics unlock the folly, and a housekeeper who is a door until she is bribed.
seed: 1

---

> north
[OK: contains "Gravel Drive"]
[OK: contains "You can see Tobias here"]

# A string topic (`about "the folly", "the fire"`) fires wherever Tobias is.
# It flips him to `shaken`, which is what unjams the folly door, and awards
# `truth worth 5`. The reply is quoted speech, so the exact form needs a fence.
> ask tobias about the folly
[OK: contains]
text
The lantern stops swinging. "Twenty years I've not opened that door, and her ladyship neither." He looks up the dark hill for a long moment. "Go on then, if you must. The door's only warped, not cursed. Shoulder it."
end text

> ask tobias about the bank
[OK: contains]
text
"Bank?" He snorts. "Bank never had it. Her ladyship trusted banks the way foxes trust hounds."
end text

# 5 points, from the folly topic alone — nothing else has scored yet.
> score
[OK: contains "You have scored 5 out of 50"]

> north
[OK: contains "Fountain Court"]

# Entering the House region fires `house-hush`; leaving the Grounds fires
# `out-of-the-wind`. Both region hooks land on the same command.
> north
[OK: contains "Entrance Hall"]
[OK: contains "You step out of the wind, and your ears sing in the sudden quiet"]
[OK: contains "The house holds its old hush"]
[OK: contains "Mrs Kettle blocks your way"]

